wAM3WWSU4sDXRHqe" class=3D"css-sdwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-=
decoration:underline;text-decoration:underline">Mayors of the World</a><spa=
n>.=E2=80=9D He told me they got fist bumps and back pats walking around to=
wn.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;ma=
rgin:0 0 15px"><span>It=E2=80=99s not just that voters know their local lea=
ders. They also have more capacity to understand and evaluate their policie=
s, Heffner said, because these policies often affect their lives in tangibl=
e ways.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#33=
3;margin:0 0 15px"><span>It reminded me of the many stories I heard from Ne=
w Yorkers about running into Mamdani out and about in the city, and also ab=
out experiencing his policies first hand. They might like the </span><a hre=
f=3D"https://nl.nytimes.com/f/newsletter/6zpqvH3vhJYnMvwFwzFhKQ~~/AAAAARA~/=
eJe8upXWvz4TTC1ejep0wBrCOMumny2LS581PhK22r5CHvZPqs4aBNTJg99rp48HsUBQp-TBvn5=
