a-8ZQbezyewwLt6IZRlNekE9S0eGSJaJL_MWDZFaZ3nWMZdK6jsyqm2GLcqa8IByN5QBF_8KyFK=
3sLZ4Ssan" class=3D"css-sdwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decorat=
ion:underline;text-decoration:underline">newly widened cycle lanes</a><span=
> around New York; they might find them frustrating. But they know who to h=
old responsible for them.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georg=
ia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>As Heffner put it: =E2=80=9CTher=
e=E2=80=99s a democratic and civic accountability that=E2=80=99s almost una=
voidable if you=E2=80=99re the mayor.=E2=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:n=
ormal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Voters feel=
 more in control. They can track the gap between what was promised and what=
=E2=80=99s been delivered.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px geor=
gia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Mayors, in other words, tend to=
 make people feel that democracy is working.</span></p><p style=3D"font:nor=
mal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font=
-weight:700">National localism=3F</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25=
px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>I spoke to Bruce Katz, w=
ho wrote =E2=80=9CThe New Localism=E2=80=9D and has advised mayors in Brita=
in and the U.S., and has also worked in national government. Katz argues lo=
cal governments not only do better at connecting with voters, but also actu=
ally govern better. Local governments often work across different departmen=
ts and the private and civic sectors in ways that national governments stru=
ggle with but that are essential for solving problems, he says.</span></p><=
p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px">=
<span>Katz wants to see more power shifted away from the national level to =
the local governments.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,=
serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>That=E2=80=99s also what Andy Burnh=
am wants.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#=
333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Burnham has gone from being the mayor of a worki=
ng-class northern region to being leader of one of the most centralized cou=
ntries in the Western world, with the vast majority of power concentrated i=
n London. But if you take him at his word, he plans to change that.</span><=
