<span>I spent last week on Skopelos, a delightful Greek island. We=E2=80=99=
d never been there before, but by Day 3 we were greeting locals =E2=80=94 V=
rahos at the local taverna, Dimitri at the boat rental. My 10-year-old hit =
it off with a group of Greek boys. We felt at home, despite being thousands=
 of kilometers away. It made me think about the amorphous nature of Europe.=
</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margi=
n:0 0 15px"><span>The continent is named after Europa, who in Greek mytholo=
gy was the first queen of Crete, another Greek island and perhaps the close=
st thing to a cradle of European civilization. Some 3,500 years later, I ca=
n take a shortish flight to more than two dozen countries with their own la=
nguages and traditions, still be in Europe, and somehow feel a sense of bel=
onging.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#33=
3;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Fittingly, I was reading =E2=80=9CHomelands: A Per=
sonal History of Europe,=E2=80=9D by Timothy Garton Ash, an Oxford historia=
n. He argues that Europe is different things to different people and depend=
ing on what definition you use, you draw its borders differently. Sometimes=
 Europe indicates a shared geography; sometimes it=E2=80=99s shared history=
; other times, it=E2=80=99s shared values.</span></p><p style=3D"font:norma=
l 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>For me, someone=
 who has lived, loved and worked in four European countries, the sense of s=
hared identity feels very real. I=E2=80=99m curious to hear from you. If yo=
u=E2=80=99re European, do you also feel =E2=80=9Cat home abroad=E2=80=9D in=
 other European countries=3F And if you=E2=80=99re not European, do you fee=
l a similar sense of shared regional identity=3F (Do you feel a sense of be=
longing in your own country, for that matter=3F) </span><a href=3D"mailto:t=
heworld@nytimes.com" class=3D"css-sdwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-te=
xt-decoration:underline;text-decoration:underline">I=E2=80=99d love to hear=
